("event/gesture" :names (":GESTURE") :kind :event :kind-name "Event" :package "LUT" :summary "Normalized input KIND :GESTURE is delivered through HANDLE-EVENT at the pointer target. EVENT-KEY is :TAP/:DOUBLETAP/:HOLD/:DRAG/:SWIPE-LEFT/:SWIPE-RIGHT/:SWIPE-UP/:SWIPE-DOWN/:PINCH-IN/:PINCH-OUT. DELTA is hold seconds or pinch angle in degrees, otherwise zero. Worker windows forward the same event fields. Devices/backend may expose a subset." :position 172853)
("event/history-overflow" :names (":HISTORY-OVERFLOW") :kind :event :kind-name "Event" :package "LUT" :summary "Standalone entry or shared TEXT-BUFFER: plist :OPERATION (:EDIT/:UNDO/:REDO), :STACK (:UNDO/:REDO), :CHARACTERS and :LIMIT after a committed range record exceeds a positive character budget and positive record limit. The destination stack is empty. Zero limits and ordinary eviction of older records are silent. Shared buffers notify after :EDIT/:CHANGE under the same reentrancy guard; standalone entries notify before the operation's :CHANGE, when applicable. Errors propagate without rolling back committed content/history." :position 173960)
("event/key" :names (":KEY") :kind :event :kind-name "Event" :package "LUT" :summary "Root window: normalized :KEY event before widget dispatch. BIND-KEY consumes a shortcut by setting EVENT-KEY to NIL. Modal dialogs suspend BIND-KEY actions." :position 175456)
